{"id":"mercy-seat","name":"Mercy Seat","aliases":[],"sources":["torrey","nave","easton"],"topics":["torrey:mercy-seat","nave:mercy-seat"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Mercy-seat","text":"(Heb. kapporeth, a “covering;” LXX. and N.T., hilasterion; Vulg., propitiatorium), the covering or lid of the ark of the covenant (q.v.). It was of acacia wood, overlaid with gold, or perhaps rather a plate of solid gold, 2 1/2 cubits long and 1 1/2 broad (Ex. 25:17; 30:6; 31:7). It is compared to the throne of grace (Heb. 9:5; Eph. 2:6). The holy of holies is called the “place of the mercy-seat” (1 Chr. 28:11: Lev. 16:2). It has been conjectured that the censer (thumiaterion, meaning “anything having regard to or employed in the burning of incense”) mentioned in Heb. 9:4 was the “mercy-seat,” at which the incense was burned by the high priest on the great day of atonement, and upon or toward which the blood of the goat was sprinkled (Lev. 16:11-16; comp. Num. 7:89 and Ex. 25:22)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3727","lemma":"כַּפֹּרֶת","xlit":"kappôreth","gloss":"a lid","kjv":"mercy seat","count":21,"share":0.47},{"strong":"H3742","lemma":"כְּרוּב","xlit":"kᵉrûwb","gloss":"a cherub or imaginary figure","kjv":"cherub, cherubims","count":15,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H727","lemma":"אָרוֹן","xlit":"ʼârôwn","gloss":"a box","kjv":"ark, chest, coffin","count":13,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H5715","lemma":"עֵדוּת","xlit":"ʻêdûwth","gloss":"testimony","kjv":"testimony, witness","count":10,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H6532","lemma":"פֹּרֶכֶת","xlit":"pôreketh","gloss":"a separatrix","kjv":"vail","count":4,"share":0.09},{"strong":"H3259","lemma":"יָעַד","xlit":"yâʻad","gloss":"to fix upon","kjv":"agree, appoint, assemble, betroth","count":4,"share":0.09}],"verses":["Exod.25.17","Exod.25.18","Exod.25.19","Exod.25.20","Exod.25.21","Exod.25.22","Exod.26.34","Exod.30.6","Exod.31.7","Exod.35.12","Exod.37.6","Exod.37.7","Exod.37.8","Exod.37.9","Exod.40.20","Lev.16.2","Lev.16.13","Lev.16.14